accounts ||--o{ audit_log_entries : actor

note bottom of account_credentials
    One optional credentials record per account; account_id is unique.
    Credentials may be absent before registration/credential setup is
    complete. Store only the Argon2id hash; never store plaintext passwords.
    failed_login_attempts and locked_until support the configured
    failed-login policy; do not assume policy values here.
    Login identifier is not defined by the brief and is not assumed
    to be an account column (AQ-04). The user approved deferring its
    selection until all-role provisioning is defined (2026-11-25);
    rationale: the brief selects no credential key. This is not team/TA
    approval. Do not fix an assumed lookup key in
    authentication persistence/API contracts.
end note

note bottom of login_sessions
    An account may have multiple sessions across different devices.
    Store only a secure hash of the random session token; never store
    the raw token. Active sessions have revoked_at IS NULL and
    expires_at later than the current time. Reject expired or revoked
    sessions. Support revoking one session and all account sessions.
    Index account_id, expires_at, and active-session lookup
    (account_id, revoked_at, expires_at).
end note

note bottom of wallets
    Available and held balances are derived from ledger entries;
    do not store a mutable balance as the source of truth. Holds
    conditionally reserve available funds atomically so simultaneous
    requests cannot make the derived balance negative.
end note

note bottom of payments
    Store exact decimal amounts and currency.
    total_amount is bill_amount plus service_fee; hold the full
    customer total as confirmed by the Sara example in Brief 2.2.
    Enforce unique (customer_account_id, idempotency_key).
    State transitions are validated by the domain model.
end note

note bottom of ledger_entries
    Ledger is append-only and stores exact Decimal values.
    A movement may contain multiple postings (for example,
    AVAILABLE debit and HELD credit for a hold). The unique
    financial_movements.idempotency_key makes the operation
    idempotent; movement_id is not unique per posting.
end note

note bottom of status_inquiry_attempts
    At most three attempts per payment (attempt numbers 1..3).
    The retry offsets are from the requirements working schedule;
    User-approved AQ-15 interpretation (2026-11-25): measure the 1, 5, and 15 minute offsets from entry into Unknown. Rationale: deterministic times from the start of the unresolved state. This records user approval, not team/TA approval.
end note

note bottom of financial_movements
    The idempotency key is stable for each logical operation.
    Populate refund_payment_id only for REFUND movements; its
    uniqueness enforces one successful refund per payment.
end note

note bottom of biller_callback_logs
    callback_fingerprint is unique per biller and identifies an
    applied callback. Duplicate deliveries are separately written
    to audit logs and never repeat a financial operation.
end note

@enduml
